<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <!-- Broad compatibility across modern .NET LTS/STS releases. -->
    <TargetFrameworks>net8.0;net9.0;net10.0</TargetFrameworks>
    <LangVersion>latest</LangVersion>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <TreatWarningsAsErrors>true</TreatWarningsAsErrors>
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
    <EnableNETAnalyzers>true</EnableNETAnalyzers>
    <AnalysisLevel>latest-recommended</AnalysisLevel>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!-- ============================ NuGet packaging metadata ============================ -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <PackageId>PostQuantum.SecureChannel</PackageId>
    <Version>1.0.0</Version>
    <AssemblyVersion>1.0.0.0</AssemblyVersion>
    <FileVersion>1.0.0.0</FileVersion>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>1.0.0: First stable release. Commits to a stable public API and wire format (protocol version 2) under Semantic Versioning — no breaking API or wire change without a major-version bump. No wire-format change from 0.3.0-preview.2. Adds a property-based no-nonce-reuse sweep across the full sequence space and key-update epochs, plus higher-order transcript-equivalence tests (closes docs/AUDIT-SCOPE.md §3 and §5). NOT INDEPENDENTLY AUDITED: an external cryptographic review of the protocol composition (handshake, key schedule, transcript binding, nonce construction, replay window) has not been performed and is not feasible at this time; the primitives are validated against published IETF/NIST test vectors, but the composition is this library's own work. The X-Wing combiner tracks draft-connolly-cfrg-xwing-kem — if the final RFC changes the combiner that will be a major-version (2.0) wire-format break handled with explicit migration guidance. See KNOWN-GAPS.md and docs/AUDIT-SCOPE.md before adopting.</PackageReleaseNotes>
    <Authors>Paul Clark</Authors>
    <Company>Paul Clark</Company>
    <Product>PostQuantum.SecureChannel</Product>
    <Description>The high-level post-quantum secure channel library for .NET. Three messages to a live session, mutually authenticated, forward-secret, replay-resistant, transport-agnostic. Built on X-Wing hybrid key agreement (ML-KEM-768 + X25519) and ML-DSA-65 signatures, with AES-256-GCM record encryption. Secure-by-default — algorithms and parameters are fixed; there are no insecure knobs. Includes a Stream adapter, DoS-resistant replay protection, NIST SP 800-38D safety bounds, and built-in observability (EventSource + Meter + ActivitySource). Use this instead of wiring primitives together by hand. Targets net8.0 / net9.0 / net10.0.</Description>
    <Summary>High-level post-quantum secure-channel library for .NET. Three-message handshake, mutually authenticated, forward-secret AES-256-GCM sessions over any transport.</Summary>
    <PackageTags>post-quantum;pqc;cryptography;x-wing;xwing;ml-kem;ml-dsa;kyber;dilithium;secure-channel;session;hybrid;kem;encryption;aes-gcm;quantum-safe;mutual-auth;tls-alternative;forward-secrecy;net10</PackageTags>
    <PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/systemslibrarian/postquantum-securechannel</PackageProjectUrl>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/systemslibrarian/postquantum-securechannel</RepositoryUrl>
    <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
    <RepositoryBranch>main</RepositoryBranch>
    <Copyright>Copyright (c) 2026 Paul Clark</Copyright>
    <PackageRequireLicenseAcceptance>false</PackageRequireLicenseAcceptance>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!-- ============================ Reproducible / source-linked builds ============================ -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <PublishRepositoryUrl>true</PublishRepositoryUrl>
    <EmbedUntrackedSources>true</EmbedUntrackedSources>
    <IncludeSymbols>true</IncludeSymbols>
    <SymbolPackageFormat>snupkg</SymbolPackageFormat>
    <Deterministic>true</Deterministic>
    <ContinuousIntegrationBuild Condition="'$(CI)' == 'true'">true</ContinuousIntegrationBuild>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- Vetted, widely-deployed implementation of ML-KEM, ML-DSA, X25519, and SHA-3/SHAKE.
         X-Wing's combiner is implemented in this library on top of those primitives. -->
    <PackageReference Include="BouncyCastle.Cryptography" Version="2.7.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.SourceLink.GitHub" Version="8.0.0" PrivateAssets="All" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="../../README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="PostQuantum.SecureChannel.Tests" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
